<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 11.6 bln levs 3-mth, coupon T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 11.6 bln levs 3-mth, coupon T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Wednesday sold 11.601 billion levs of three-month, floater coupon T-bills, yielding 56.36 percent to maturity, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the central bank's main interest rate, now set at 17.14 percent monthly or 205.68 percent annually.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry. Auction date and issue date overlap.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Price in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3025497028</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon</p>
<p> Term			    three months</p>
<p> Issue date		    April 9</p>
<p> Maturity date		 July 9</p>
<p> Bids received		 12,301 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.69</p>
<p> Bids approved		 11,601 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.75 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     56.36 pct</p>
<p>@</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
